// wdoc section: Overview.
page wdoc_overview { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "wdoc Overview"

  p "wdoc is WCL's documentation generator. A `.wcl` source file declares one or more `site`s and `page`s; `wcl wdoc build` renders the pages to static HTML, and `wcl wdoc serve` runs a watch+rebuild dev server. This very book is built with it."

  h2 "Build & serve"

  code bash {
    source = <<'BASH'
wcl wdoc build docs/main.wcl --out docs/_site
wcl wdoc serve docs/main.wcl                       # http://127.0.0.1:8080
wcl wdoc serve docs/main.wcl --addr 127.0.0.1:3000 # custom address
wcl wdoc build docs/main.wcl --out _site --site docs   # filter to one site
BASH
  }

  h2 "Multi-site routing"

  p "A document can declare several `site` blocks. The site with `root = true` renders at the output root (`/`); other sites render into per-site subdirectories (`/<site>/`). A `chooser` index is auto-generated when no site is rooted."

  callout "Prelude is auto-imported" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "wcl wdoc build prepends import <wdoc/prelude.wcl> for you, so page / text / code / callout / table / h1..h6 / diagram and every other stdlib block is already in scope. Author source files have no prelude line."
  }

  h2 "Authoring shape"

  p "Most pages look like this: a `page <name>` block holding text, headings, callouts, code blocks, tables, and (occasionally) diagrams or charts. See [Pages](wdoc_pages) for the page block's fields and [Sites & Templates](wdoc_sites) for how a site is wired up."
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
page index { sites = [:mysite]  start = true
  h1 "My project"
  p "Welcome — see [the docs](docs)."
}
WCL
  }

  p "Next: [Sites & Templates](wdoc_sites)."
}
